# ============================================================================
# comfyui-backup config — copy to "config.env" (gitignored) and adjust.
# Sourced by install.sh, download-models.sh and serve.sh.
# ============================================================================

# Where ComfyUI itself is checked out. Deliberately OUTSIDE this repo: its
# models/ subtree holds tens of GB and must never be committed, and ComfyUI
# insists on finding models relative to its own directory.
COMFY_DIR="$HOME/.local/share/comfyui/ComfyUI"

# Network bind. 0.0.0.0 is required, not cosmetic: the Hermes agent runs in a
# Docker container and reaches the host over a bridge gateway (172.20.0.1 on
# Gertrude), so a 127.0.0.1 bind would be invisible to it.
COMFY_HOST="0.0.0.0"
COMFY_PORT="8188"

# PyTorch wheel index and a PINNED version. Both matter, and the window is
# narrow (found by trying, 2026-09-24 on driver 535.309.01 = CUDA 12.2):
#   * ComfyUI's requirements.txt does not pin torch at all, so pip takes the
#     newest the chosen index offers.
#   * cu121 tops out at torch 2.5.1, and cu124 at 2.6.0 — both too OLD:
#     comfy_kitchen registers a custom op annotated `stride: list[int]`, and
#     torch's infer_schema rejects PEP 585 builtins until 2.7.
#   * The newest torch from plain PyPI is too NEW: it refuses to initialise
#     CUDA with "driver is too old (found version 12020)".
#   * torch 2.7.1+cu126 satisfies both. Verified: cuda.is_available() is True
#     and `import comfy_kitchen` succeeds.
# Raise COMFY_TORCH_VERSION only together with a driver upgrade, and re-test
# both conditions rather than assuming.
COMFY_TORCH_INDEX="https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu126"
COMFY_TORCH_VERSION="2.7.1"

# Which GPU PyTorch may use. The AMD card is not a CUDA device at all, so this
# cannot collide with llama.cpp — index 0 is the RTX 3060 and the only entry.
COMFY_CUDA_DEVICE="0"

# Empty on purpose: NO --lowvram. That flag pins the text encoder to the CPU
# (comfy/model_management.py text_encoder_device()), which cost ~48 s of every
# edit job once the Lightning LoRA had cut sampling to 4 steps. Without it the
# encoder runs on the GPU and ComfyUI swaps it against the diffusion model:
# edit 75 s -> 45-49 s, text-to-image 34 s -> 20-34 s, peak 11465 MiB
# (2026-11-01, see README). The 2026-09-24 result that favoured --lowvram was
# 20 steps at cfg 2.5, where sampling dominated. Dynamic VRAM, the other way to
# get the encoder onto the GPU, needs torch >= 2.8, which driver 535 rules out.
COMFY_EXTRA_ARGS=""

# Optional: HuggingFace token for gated downloads (or run 'hf auth login').
HF_TOKEN=""
